[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug, one fix queued. Read the reports, not the subjects,
and it holds three problems. The queued parser fix closes only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one issue. The parser fix leaves the booking-v3 hint and the one-day move open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

**1 · `parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first** (<ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" /> reports).
Our tenants write the day first. The parser reads month first, so day and month swap:
"Our 7 April reminder went out on 4 July." It happens on every channel, for every
day-first tenant. This is what #4471 was opened for, and the fix queued for it.

**2 · `hint`: the booking-v3 form tells people to type month first** (<ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" /> reports).
Under its date field booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. People at day-first tenants do what the
hint says, and the form then reads the date their tenant's way, day first. The dates swap, so
these look like the parser bug, but they come only through the form, only at booking-v3
tenants (alder.physio, pale.harbour, copper.studio). Fixing the parser does not change the
hint. The fix is the form's hint.

**3 · `one-day`: the date moves by one day** (<ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="one-day" /> reports).
No swap of day and month moves a date by one day. "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says
Monday 11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." "Every booking in
June is one day off." This is a time-zone or summer-time shift, not the parser. The desk had
already marked these reports (`desk-notes.json`), but #4471 still counts them under `parser`.

## Why one ticket hid three

- **Merged as one, read as one.** Reports with many different subject lines went into #4471.
  Neither the subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) nor "it is about
  dates" tells the causes apart. Only the body and the tenant do.
- **Intake tags are a guess from the browser.** An `en-US` browser got `hint`, the rest
  `parser`. The cause is the tenant and the way in, so the tag column above disagrees with the
  problem column in both directions.
- **The export repeats rows.** Pages of the export overlap. Count each report id once.

## What to do

1. Keep #4471 for the parser. Close it when the parser fix ships and new `parser` reports stop.
2. Fix the booking-v3 hint (issue #2 in the tracker). Do not wait for the parser fix.
3. Hand the one-day move (issue #3) to whoever owns time zones in `sched-prod`. It needs its
   own reproduction: a meeting seen from two time zones, and a booking across the summer-time change.
4. Split by what the body shows when a big ticket grows. Subject alone merges different bugs.

Counts on this page are built from the export at render time. When the desk adds reports or
marks more one-day moves, the numbers follow.

